  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Ezogelin corbasi sits somewhere between mercimek corbasi and a thick grain soup. Red lentils provide a smooth, dissolving base while fine bulgur adds body and a gentle nuttiness. Tomato puree and paprika give it a warm, orange-red colour and a depth that plain lentil soup does not quite reach."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The soup is filling in a quiet way. A bowl of it with good bread is a complete meal. A squeeze of lemon at the end is not optional; it cuts through the richness and ties everything together."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Fine bulgur is essential here rather than coarse bulgur, which would take much longer to cook. Most Turkish or Middle Eastern grocery shops stock it; it may be labelled number 1 or fine-ground."
          }
        ]
      },
